hunmin (0.3.0~rc) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.3 prerelease: automatic Hangul/English switch (docs/SPEC-MODES.md
    R1-R15, E1-E8). The engine judges at the composition boundary, each
    frontend performs the switch, and with the option off the layer
    delivers exactly what 0.2 delivered.
  * The switch is refused, not defaulted, where its data package is
    absent: hunmin-en-us ships separately and the option stays disabled
    until it is installed.
  * The han/yeong key: a single press switches manually, modifier + the
    key addresses the special-function namespace; the engine names the
    chord and every frontend's settings surface reads the state back.
  * Prerelease versioning: the package says 0.3.0~rc so it sorts before
    the 0.3.0 release; the Android build says 0.3.0-rc with versionCode 3.

 -- Seo Bon Keun <scobyseo@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 19:25:00 +0900

hunmin (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Windows TSF frontend (milestone 0.2): the TIP builds with MSVC and
    registers through its own DllRegisterServer (CLSID, CTF TIP tree,
    Korean language profile, categories), composes inline through the
    shared buffering layer, serves Hanja candidates from the bundled
    tables, and ships a WinUI 3 settings surface.
  * Windows installation package: hunmin-0.2.0-setup.exe (Inno Setup),
    static CRT so a clean image needs no VC redist, data staged beside
    the DLL, Start-menu entry, uninstall that mirrors registration.
  * The TIP declares GUID_TFCAT_TIPCAP_SYSTRAYSUPPORT, so the Win11 input
    indicator gives it an entry of its own; GetIcon serves the per-mode
    badge and the entry's click launches the settings exe.
  * fcitx5 addon: engine, layout tables and behaviour fixes since 0.1.
  * Android: same feature set, rebuilt against the 0.2.0 engine.

 -- Seo Bon Keun <scobyseo@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:20:00 +0900

hunmin (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. libhunmin Hangul input engine (layouts as data,
    libhangul parity sweep + golden vectors), 신세벌식 P2 support,
    hunmin-sim trace tool, and the fcitx5 addon with an in-process
    tier-D1 test.

